End a pairing attempt when it finishes, fails, or its client disconnects.

Pending pairing entries stayed in memory after pairing completed, failed, or
dropped before a PIN was entered, keeping cancelled requests listed for five
minutes and causing /submit-pin without a uniqueid to return 409 Conflict when
another client tried to pair. Adds a salt-matched PairingGuard, removes finished
attempts in check_client_pairing_secret without touching waiting (key=None)
entries, releases the write lock before RSA verification and disk writes, and
clears post-PIN attempts on /unpair.

Not upstream yet.

